extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts World Book 4: Africa, printed 118-119 (cache p119-p120). The
    heading and the whole entry are on printed 119, which was rendered and
    read; printed 118 carries the end of the Agogwe and the Tree People
    introduction. Printed 120 is Ethiopia and holds nothing of this class, so
    the range stops at 119 (the brief said 118-120).
  - XP: the "Tree People, Pygmy Hunter & Tautons" ladder, printed 160, read off
    a render. Lower bounds stored as printed. Level 2 is printed
    1,935-3,870, repeating level 1''s upper bound; stored as 1935 AS PRINTED.
    Level 11 is printed 110,001-140,000 although level 10 ends at 110,500;
    stored as printed (110001), still strictly rising.
  - POOLS: the book prints no hit point or S.D.C. formula; "+15 S.D.C. ... in
    addition to possible attribute and skill bonuses" is a pool bonus. No
    sdc_base or mdc_base, so men_of_arms: false, as for every race. P.P.E.
    3D6. No starting money ("Money: None").
  - SKILLS: the R.C.C. prints its own "O.C.C. Related" and secondary skill
    lists and takes no separate O.C.C., so both are stored (the Grimbor and
    Shaydor precedent). Related: three, plus two at level 2 and one at 4, 8
    and 12. Secondary: three at level 3 and three at level 8 (count 0 at
    creation). Pygmy and Swahili have no catalog rows: one choose-2 from
    Language: Other at a fixed 85 (two fixed Language: Other entries would
    collapse into one skill by name). Gobblely and Euro fixed at 85, native
    tongue 98. Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals 20+10. Identify Plants &
    Fruits is Identify Plants & Fruit 25+15. Land Navigation stored at the
    jungle figure, 36+15; the +5% elsewhere is in the note. W.P. Targeting
    "(60% use throwing sticks and spears, 40% bows & arrows)" is a choice of
    W.P. Targeting or W.P. Archery, a judgement call. Running''s own bonuses
    come from its catalog row and are not added to the class.
  - HAND TO HAND: Expert, "other hand to hand combat skills are not
    available" is costs: {}. Females and non-hunter-warriors have Basic; a
    variant cannot take a granted skill away, so that is prose (restrictions
    and the skill note).
  - RELATED CATEGORY LIMITS: Pilot "horsemanship, water vessels and hover
    vehicles only" is Horsemanship: General and Exotic Animals plus the boat,
    water-scooter and hover rows (judgement; the knightly and Cyber-Knight
    riding rows are left out). Rogue excludes Computer Hacking, Streetwise and
    Streetwise: Drugs. Technical "lore and language only" is every Language
    and Lore row in the Technical category on 2026-09-26 except Native Tongue
    and Language Dialects; a row added later is not reached.
  - BONUSES: +1 attack, +2 initiative, +3 save vs poisons (toxins_poisons)
    and disease, +15 S.D.C., stored unconditionally. The +3 dodge during a
    running leap is conditional and is in the Glide ability.
  - PSIONICS: psionics_allowed: false, because the book fixes the race''s
    psionics rather than leaving them to the random table. Sense supernatural
    evil "identical to the dog boys" is a natural ability pointing at the Dog
    Boy''s Sense Supernatural Beings; the Africa book prints no numbers for it.
    The 10% who are master psionics with healing powers are NOT MODELLED: the
    book gives no I.S.P., power count or progression, a variant cannot carry
    psionics, and an ability choice would have to invent those numbers. It is
    prose in natural_abilities.
  - EQUIPMENT: rope (10 ft, one 20-foot catalog length), small sack and a
    wooden spear are stored. The rope belt has no row. The war club (2D6
    S.D.C.) or 1D4 wooden throwing sticks (1D6 S.D.C.) have no Rifts gear
    row and are prose. The 40% with modern amenities, the 10% with a
    vibro-knife, neuro-mace, laser scalpel, handgun or tool, and the 15% with
    magic items are percentile rolls and are prose.
  - Attributes as printed: I.Q. 3D6, M.A. 4D6, M.E. 3D6, P.S. 3D4, P.P. 3D6,
    P.E. 3D6, P.B. 3D6, Spd 4D6.
