# Tree People

## Lore

The Tree People are tiny, fur-covered D-bees, probably from another
dimension, who have flourished in the forests of Africa, above all in the
Congo and to a lesser degree Uganda and Kenya. They stand about three feet
tall, with huge bush-baby eyes and leathery flying-squirrel membranes under
the arms, and they are highly intelligent and extraordinarily agile. They eat
insects, birds and eggs, small animals, fruit, berries and leaves gathered in
the trees.

They live in treetop villages of anything from a few hundred to a few thousand,
led by a war chief who also runs the hunt, a wise man who is in effect a
medicine man or healer, and a council of elders. They have no priests or rain
makers, but some are effectively druids or herbalists. Unlike the agogwe they
see themselves as one nation, call one another brother and sister, and the
tribes will join together against a common enemy. As many as six million are
thought to live in Africa.

Normally gentle, playful and full of laughter, they never war among
themselves, but they show little mercy to enemies. Slavers, including the
minions of the Splugorth and Rama-Set, are hated and driven from the jungle,
and the harm of any tree person, agogwe or pygmy is avenged. Their worst
crimes are betraying their people to foreigners and murder, punished by
banishment forever; imprisonment is never used, for they are obsessed with
freedom.

Their curiosity is insatiable. Young hunter-warriors will drop into a
stranger''s camp to ask questions, and they are notorious for rummaging
through foreigners'' belongings, playing with their weapons and radios, and
carrying off sweets and trinkets to share with the tribe. They are just as
famous for warning travelers of danger, leaving food for the lost, healing
the sick and freeing people from bondage. They regard the Congo as theirs and
all outsiders as suspicious foreigners; their only true allies are the
pygmies and the agogwe.

## GM Notes

About 10% of tree people are master psionics with healing powers. The book
gives no figures for them; decide the I.S.P. and powers for such a character
before play. 40% carry a few modern items (canteen, utility belt, sunglasses
or tinted goggles, air filter, infrared distancing binoculars, mirror, small
knives and tools), 10% a vibro-knife, neuro-mace, laser scalpel, handgun or
tool, and 15% magic pygmy charms, talismans or Millennium Tree items. Most
other goods, clothes and electronics are regarded as useless junk. Their
typical weapons are a war club (2D6 S.D.C.) or 1D4 wooden throwing sticks
(1D6 S.D.C.) and/or a spear.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'tree-people');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'tree-people';

